meta {
  name: Supabase Login
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{supabase_url}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  apikey: {{supabase_anon_key}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "phobosmailbox@unwita.com",
    "password": "your-password-here"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    const data = res.getBody();
    if (data.access_token) {
      bru.setEnvVar("token", data.access_token);
      console.log("Token saved to environment variable 'token'");
    }
  }
}

docs {
  # Supabase Login

  Authenticates a user with Supabase using email and password credentials.
  **After successful login, the access_token is automatically saved to the `token` environment variable.**

  ## Request Body Fields
  - `email` (required): User's email address
  - `password` (required): User's password

  ## Response
  - 200: Login Successful
    - Returns `access_token` (JWT token for API authentication)
    - Returns `refresh_token` (for token renewal)
    - Returns `user` object with user details
  - 400: Bad Request - Invalid email or password format
  - 401: Unauthorized - Invalid credentials

  ## Usage
  1. Update the email and password in the request body
  2. Run this request
  3. On success, the `token` variable is automatically updated
  4. All other requests will use the new token automatically

  ## Note
  The access token is a JWT that includes:
  - `sub`: User ID (used for last_updated_by fields)
  - `email`: User's email
  - `app_metadata.role`: User's role (admin, op_manager, appraiser)

  Token expires after 1 hour. Run this request again to get a new token.
}
